a motorcyclist is dead and a juvenile is  in custody after a fatal accident in the  southwest part of town the victim  identified as 59-year-old kenneth lee  barker the young driver police say  showed signs of impairment at the scene  8 news now reporter sally jaramillo  joins us near patrick and tanea with  more on how barker is being remembered  sally  kirsten a memorial is going for kenneth  lee barker he is described as a great  guy who loved motorcycles and had a  heart of gold all the neighbors left and  shunked as he only lived a block away  it's a really sad day here in patrick  and tanea it all happened yesterday  evening las vegas metro police say  witnesses told them a honda accord  driven by a juvenile speeding eastbound  on patrick the young driver moved into  oncoming lanes to pass another vehicle  when suddenly they collided with a  motorcycle the victim's neighbors can't  believe it i just heard him leave  his house and then all of a sudden a few  minutes later i hear sirens and it's  like no it can't be robert f sober is  kenneth's neighbor he says he lived  behind him and was truly an amazing guy  who loved to ride motorcycles and was a  big nascar fan ken was a great guy and  to have somebody you know he's barely 60  years old to lose his life  he's going to the store  you know it's ridiculous that people  think they can just do whatever they  want sober says it's devastating to know  he's no longer with them this  neighborhood over here a lot of people  drive down patrick at excessive speeds  it's a 25 mile an hour zone and every  day i sit in my garage and i can see  people going by doing 60  70 miles an hour and says people need to  slow down ask for that juvenile it's  unacceptable he's going to pay for it  and it's sad that a young kid his whole  life is  totally changed due to one choice of  drinking and driving  charges have not been announced for the  juvenile police say the driver did show  signs of impairment i'm told kenneth has  a son and he is  definitely a grandparent as well and  that the community his neighbors are  currently working on creating a vigil  for him sally jaramillo live local now
 

